%SIXMD 1
# @?DATE - DISPLAY OR SET UTC DATE AND TIME

## DESCRIPTION

DATE READS THE DAIMOS WALL CLOCK AND PRINTS THE UTC CALENDAR DATE AND TIME.
IF THE CLOCK IS NOT YET SET, DATE PROMPTS FOR THE INITIAL UTC VALUE.
THE EXPLICIT COMMAND 'DATE SET' ALSO PROMPTS FOR A NEW UTC VALUE.

ENTER TIME AS 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' USING A FOUR-DIGIT YEAR AND 24-HOUR
UTC. SUPPORTED YEARS ARE 2026 THROUGH 2125. DATE REJECTS IMPOSSIBLE
DATES, INCLUDING INVALID LEAP DAYS.

SETTING TIME REQUIRES ROOT PRIVILEGES AND A SOFTWARE WALL CLOCK. A
PRESENT PHYSICAL PCLK IS READ-ONLY AND CANNOT BE SET USING DATE.

LOGIN OFFERS DATE BEFORE STARTING THE ROOT SHELL IF UTC IS UNSET.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - SUCCESS
### @?1 - OPERATION FAILED OR CONDITION FALSE
### @?2 - INVALID USAGE WHEN APPLICABLE
